🐝 Hivemind notes 🐝

For this season, a small group (now 8) have banded together for the @Jumpthewave predictions to have a group think each GW. 

Everyone is set on the back 4. As for the midfield and forward lines, or a blend of both really, we can see all of Szoboszlai, Mac Allister, Wirtz and Barcola starting. Most think Koumas will get the nod and Munoz too. We have all said the same things though - we could see false 9s in Szoboszlai and Wirtz with a Gravenberch/Nyoni starting behind. We’ve considered Ngumoha starting too. It really is a tough call this week. 

The majority are siding with Koumas through the middle! 

Some paraphrased comments from the predicting team: 

@FPL__Lad - “There are a few main talking points this week. The main ones are Isak and Gakpo being ruled out of the game. A massive blow for us. I expect it to be a straight swap of Koumas in for Isak rather than Wirtz going in there and a change around in midfield etc. Koumas's high pressing will be a key point imo. If he does start I'm very excited to see how he gets on. A 50/50 for me on the right between Munoz and Rio but I would go Munoz given he looks the most comfortable out of the pair on the right-hand side.”

“For me the pivot of Mac and Szobo stays too.”

@thomas_toner22 - “My 11. With Isak and Gakpo out, Koumas deserves an opportunity and seems like he will get one given how much Iraola continues to praise him. Wouldn’t be surprised if Rio on the right”

@stephenm6464 - “…decisions of note I’ve made is Nyoni and Macca pivot with Wirtz and Szoboszlai as two false nines and Munoz off the right. No strong feelings and could easily see 2 of Gravenberch/Ngumoha/Koumas instead”

@FPL_Baldie - “Koumas was mentioned by Iraola. I think this is the most obvious shout here”

“I would give rio the lask away game in the ucl”

Thank you 

@stephenm6464 
@FPL_Baldie 
@InshallahSalah
@Anfieldman94 
@FPL__Lad 
@YashAsthana87 & 
@thomas_toner22 

for all your work this week 👏🏼

